  "note": "Scratching a hole: chest dropped, rump up, nose down over the work, and the forepaws alternating a four-beat rake -- reach out, set down, pull back through the dirt, lift clear. Head pitch is POSITIVE here because positive is nose-down; `alert` raises its head with a negative one. This cannot be a gait even though it cycles, because a gait moves every planted foot at one ground speed and here the forepaws rake backwards while the hind feet stand still -- hence `unweighted`, which says the forepaws work at ground level without carrying the animal. Two full strokes per leg, half a cycle apart so one paw is always down, and the last key repeats the first so it loops.",
